From: devcore94 <ditternation@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelsu: start module services after Android FBE unlock

Android 17 no longer reliably triggers the legacy nonencrypted or
vold.decrypt=trigger_restart_framework actions. Run the KernelSU service
stage when user 0 credential-encrypted storage becomes available so module
service.sh scripts are activated before boot completion.

diff --git a/drivers/kernelsu/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c b/drivers/kernelsu/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c
--- a/drivers/kernelsu/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c
+++ b/drivers/kernelsu/kernel/runtime/ksud_integration.c
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@ static const char KERNEL_SU_RC[] =
 	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " services\n"
 	"\n"
 
+	"on property:sys.user.0.ce_available=true\n"
+	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " services\n"
+	"\n"
+
 	"on property:sys.boot_completed=1\n"
 	"    exec u:r:" KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN ":s0 root -- " KSUD_PATH " boot-completed\n"
 	"\n"
